{"id":"181c715a-9c2b-48cd-97e6-db1a00777599","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The Java entry point 'main' is always invoked with a non-null String array.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-17T15:24:36.768974Z"}
{"id":"be71e3f6-e689-4bfd-9d8d-6a2345d5e53c","expr":"b <= 0 || a / b == a / b","rationale":"Division by zero must be guarded; if b is zero, integer division is not performed in the method. This ensures a / b is only evaluated when safe.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-17T15:24:36.770345Z"}
{"id":"e1987e73-e43f-475f-9045-325ce231ad1e","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The 'args' array, as per the Java main(String[]) contract, should not be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-17T15:24:36.769015Z"}
{"id":"37b67ddf-160f-45be-bd34-055c9c2b264b","expr":"true || b != 0","rationale":"There are no constraints on parameters at entry; both a and b can take any int value.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-17T15:24:36.770345Z"}
{"id":"b71ee738-1eb4-45aa-a8a1-6cb9746c33bd","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"In Java, arrays always have a non-negative length.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-17T15:24:36.768974Z"}
{"id":"8a9ea95c-9624-49d4-8388-d3f1ff7a2079","expr":"a == 0 || b != 0 || a / b == 0","rationale":"If a is 0, a / b would be zero if b != 0; if b is zero, division is not performed.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-17T15:24:36.770345Z"}
{"id":"283ae84e-31c8-48e2-8a9f-902eee79bdd4","expr":"(b == 0) == (result == Integer.MIN_VALUE)","rationale":"If and only if b is zero, the result is Integer.MIN_VALUE.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-17T15:24:36.771283Z"}
{"id":"c9799e2d-f85c-4a04-8d6b-65053373ff6a","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"Arrays in Java have non-negative length.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-17T15:24:36.769015Z"}
{"id":"acca0703-131c-4d87-b41a-a9e213424096","expr":"(b != 0) == (result == a / b)","rationale":"If and only if b is not zero, the result is a / b.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-17T15:24:36.771283Z"}
{"id":"fead7e1c-c6d9-42d6-8ab6-ea8c46e74946","expr":"((b != 0) && (result * b == a - (a % b)))","rationale":"If b is not zero, result equals a/b, hence result*b equals a minus the remainder of integer division.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-17T15:24:36.771283Z"}
{"id":"a6cecee5-05cf-4004-9db0-af27f2f392ec","expr":"(result == Integer.MIN_VALUE) || (b != 0)","rationale":"If result is not Integer.MIN_VALUE, then b must not be zero.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-17T15:24:36.771283Z"}
{"id":"73d341a8-3018-4b2c-816f-c31e30d31ff2","expr":"(b == 0) || (result == a / b)","rationale":"If b is not zero, result must be a / b; otherwise, b is zero.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-17T15:24:36.771283Z"}
